---
source: tests/cli_help_snapshot_tests.rs
description: gpy --help
expression: help
---
Fast, cross-platform agent for Git status and language detection used by the GPY prompt for Bash, Fish, and Zsh

Usage: gpy <COMMAND>

Commands:
  start        Start the background agent
  stop         Stop the background agent
  restart      Restart the background agent
  status       Show agent status and diagnostics
  theme        Manage themes
  palette      Manage palettes (color themes)
  plugin       Manage plugins
  enable       Enable a prompt segment
  disable      Disable a prompt segment
  segments     List all available segments
  lang         Language detection configuration
  config       Configuration management
  doctor       Run health checks and diagnostics
  debug        Debugging tools
  setup        Wire GPY into your shell (Fish, Zsh or Bash): install its scripts, add the rc-file block, and pick an icon style. Safe to re-run
  completions  Generate shell completions
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

Exit status: 0 success; 1 failure (one `Error:` line on stderr); 2 usage error.
status: 0 running (or busy); 3 not running; 4 not answering or unknown.
start, restart: 6 disabled by agent.enabled = false.
doctor: 1 only when a check failed.
